iconductor software solutions; KLA Pro systems; and specialty semiconductor manufacturing, benchtop metrology, surface characterization, material strength characterization, and electrical property measurement products. It also provides etch, plasma dicing, deposition and other wafer processing technologies and solutions; direct imaging, inspection, optical shaping, inkjet, and additive printing, as well as computer-aided manufacturing and engineering solutions; and components. In addition, the company offers service programs. It serves semiconductor, and semiconductor-related and electronic device manufacturers. The company operates in China, Taiwan, Korea, North America, Japan, Europe, Israel, and rest of Asia. The company was formerly known as KLA-Tencor Corporation and changed its name to KLA Corporation in July 2019. KLA Corporation was incorporated in 1975 and is headquartered in Milpitas, California.","employees":17000,"website":"https://www.kla.com","country":"United States","city":"Milpitas","officers":[{"name":"Mr. Richard P. Wallace","title":"President, CEO & Executive Director"},{"name":"Mr. Bren D. Higgins","title":"Executive VP & CFO"},{"name":"Ms. Mary Beth Wilkinson","title":"Executive VP, Chief Legal Officer & Corporate Secretary"}]},"sector_medians":{"fpe":16.44,"tpe":27.86,"ps":4.209,"pfcf":25.47,"peg":1.06,"pb":4.445,"ev_ebitda":18.23,"rev_growth":0.1935,"eps_growth":0.3785,"eps_growth_fwd":0.2571,"eps_growth_next":0.1802,"div_yield":0,"roe":0.1241,"roa":0.04991,"de":32.04,"gross_margin":0.5374,"op_margin":0.118,"profit_margin":0.09496,"current_ratio":1.867},"valuation":[{"k":"fpe","label":"Forward P/E","v":20.12,"sector":16.44,"verdict":"Fairly valued"},{"k":"tpe","label":"TTM P/E","v":35.83,"sector":27.86,"verdict":"Overvalued"},{"k":"ps","label":"Price / Sales","v":12.82,"sector":4.209,"verdict":"Overvalued"},{"k":"pfcf","label":"Price / FCF","v":66.03,"sector":25.47,"verdict":"Overvalued"},{"k":"peg","label":"PEG","v":1.3,"sector":1.06,"verdic